%% Push without content on iOS or macOS with Notification Service Extension (NSE).
%% Domain details: 13-push-notifications.md and 15-client-architecture.md.
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  box worker
    participant NV as notify consumer
    participant J as River job notify.push_send
  end
  participant DB as PostgreSQL
  participant APNS as APNs
  participant OS as iOS
  participant NSE as Notification Service Extension
  participant API as api node
  participant APP as App

  NV->>DB: lock consumer row push, read events from cursor (message.created)
  NV->>NV: determine recipients, per recipient authorize(push.deliver, thread)
  NV->>DB: insert jobs per active push registration, advance cursor, COMMIT
  J->>APNS: HTTP/2: placeholder text, mutable-content, only thread_id and message_id
  alt token invalid
    APNS-->>J: error for the device
    J->>DB: push_registrations: disabled_at, disabled_reason token_invalid
  else accepted
    APNS-->>J: 200, set last_success_at
    APNS-)OS: push
    OS->>NSE: start extension with limited execution time
    NSE->>NSE: credentials from the shared keychain of the app group, DPoP proof with device key
    NSE->>API: GET messages/{id} (DPoP)
    API->>API: authorize(recipient, message.read, message)
    alt allowed and reachable
      API-->>NSE: 200 message
      NSE->>OS: replace title and text (truncated)
    else 404, no connection or time expired
      NSE->>OS: leave the neutral placeholder unchanged
    end
    OS->>OS: show notification
    OS->>APP: tap opens deep link to thread and message
    APP->>API: load thread, advance read state
  end
